<title>USA: Volkswagen sees U.S. '97 sales up 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Volkswagen sees U.S. '97 sales up 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen of America Inc expects a 25 percent gain in U.S. sales this year, its chief executive said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we could be 25 percent better than we did last year,&quot; Clive Warrilow, president and chief executive officer of Volkswagen AG's U.S. unit, said at the North American International Auto Show.</p>
<p>Last year, the company sold 135,907 cars in the United States, an 18 percent increase over the previous year. It was the German-based automaker best U.S. sales performance since 1990 when it had sales of 136,357.</p>
</text>
